  Three functions are included, in omni_extract_bench/values.py and marked there:
  `canonical` (as `_fold_cosmetic`), `unwrap`, and `_drop_datalab_sidecars`. They were
  copied rather than reimplemented so that scores produced here would remain identical to the
  upstream metric on the same inputs.

  `_fold_cosmetic` has since DIVERGED, in two places, each marked `DIVERGENCE FROM
  UPSTREAM` in the source with its evidence. Upstream strips whitespace, commas, hyphens and
  periods from anywhere in a value, and strips leading zeros inside every digit run. Both
  destroy content rather than spelling on this corpus -- `A-01` == `A01`, `5.2.1.5` == `5215`,
  the swim times `1:00.50` == `1:50`, the concentrations `0.11%w/w` == `1.1%w/w` == `11%w/w`,
  and `INV-007` == `INV-7`. Whitespace and commas are still folded everywhere; a period only
  when trailing; hyphens and leading zeros are kept. `unwrap` and `_drop_datalab_sidecars`
  remain verbatim.

  The full grader was vendored at omni_extract_bench/vendor/longextract_bench/ until these
  three were the only parts still reachable from the scoring path. Nothing else from it is
  used: this repo scores through omni_extract_bench/score.py alone.
